  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 329 AM CDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nStrong west-northwest flow continues as we head into midweek, with \nat least some threat for thunderstorms continuing as well. This \nstrong flow aloft will keep ample deep layer shear in place both \nWednesday and Thursday, and some threat for strong to severe storms \nappears possible. Confidence in both placement and coverage of \nstorms remains low confidence for now, and trends will continue to \nbe monitored. By late week, upper ridging will begin to establish \nacross the Rockies, amplifying into the weekend. This upper ridge \naxis also begins to translate eastwards into the Plains by Saturday \nnight. This will lead to height rises across the area and increasing \ntemperatures into the weekend. This could also bring a brief \nreprieve from thunderstorm threats, before the ridge begins to \nflatten early next week and zonal flow establishes aloft again.",
